# =============================================================================
# operator.v1.OperatorService — NOT REACHABLE FROM THIS COLLECTION
#
#   make api-check      validate the paths below against api/proto
#   make api-operator   open this file (nvim) — see docs/http-collections.md
#
# Why nothing here is runnable: OperatorService is served by the release-orchestrator
# **agent gateway**, a separate TLS listener whose identity comes from the client
# certificate (`cmd/orchestrator/main.go`, `operator.NewCertificateIdentityHandler`;
# ADR-001/ADR-018). It is deliberately not exposed on the plain management port, so
# a Kulala collection cannot present the operator certificate and enrollment token
# the gateway requires — and the mTLS port is not the same as the operator agent's
# own local listener.
#
# The four RPCs and their real authentication path:
#   Enroll                    enrollment token (one-time), no client certificate yet
#   RenewCertificate          verified client certificate; renew invalidates the old serial
#   CommandStream             verified client certificate; long-lived bidi stream
#   GetActiveOperatorSession  verified client certificate
#
# Reachable evidence for these lives in the Go tests and the staged E2E gates
# (make install-sdk / upgrade-sdk / rollout-watch), not in api/kulala.
# Contract reference:
#   api/proto/operator/v1/operator.proto
#
# If a runnable probe is needed, point it at the gateway with a client
# certificate — for example:
#   openssl s_client -connect localhost:30084 -cert agent.crt -key agent.key \
#     -CAfile data/dev-ca/ca.crt -quiet
# and keep that out of the tracked collection: the certificate and key are
# per-operator secrets.
